                          1. TOOL OVERVIEW
================================================================================

  This is a Python-based HTML protection tool that compresses and encodes
  HTML code using Zlib compression and Base64 encoding. It creates a
  self-extracting HTML file that can be opened in any modern browser.

  How it works:
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  1. User pastes HTML code
  2. Code is compressed using Zlib (level 6)
  3. Compressed data is Base64 encoded
  4. A wrapper HTML file is created
  5. Browser decompresses and displays the original code

  Perfect for:
  ✓ Protecting your HTML source code
  ✓ Reducing file size
  ✓ Obfuscating code from casual viewers
  ✓ Creating self-extracting HTML archives

